parameters.description:
**A reed.co.uk job search page or employer listing address, pasted as-is.** Required.

- a keyword / place page with its filters (`https://www.reed.co.uk/jobs/nurse-jobs-in-leeds?…`);
- the all-jobs page (`/jobs`) or a search-box address (`/jobs?keywords=nurse&location=leeds`);
- an employer's listing (`/jobs/tradewind-recruitment/p12807` or `…/o427940`).

**Lenient pastes:** send `url` URL-encoded or not (unencoded query parts are read back into it). A missing
scheme, a `www.`, bare or `m.` host, quotes or a label around it, trailing punctuation, a Markdown, Slack or Jira link,
percent-encoding and text after the address are all read. The address ends at the first space, line break or `|`; a
line break that plainly cuts it is joined back.

**Refused with a 400** that names what to use instead:

- another site; a job page (→ `/job-details-by-url`), company profile (→ `/company-profile-by-url`) or course page;
- a bare number (a job_id → `/job-details`);
- two different Reed addresses (the same one twice counts once), or an address broken off;
- code-like text (``, `javascript:`), or an employer or location id outside 1 - 2,147,483,647.

On an employer listing the path names the employer  -  another employer id in the query is ignored.

