parameters.description:
**A reed.co.uk course listing address, pasted as-is.** Required.

- subject, keyword and filtered pages (`https://www.reed.co.uk/courses/python/online`, `/courses/accounting/level-3`);
- provider listings (`/courses/janets/p1778`) and place pages (`/courses/first-aid-training/leeds`);
- search-box addresses (`/courses/all?keywords=python`); the listing's own sort and page size are kept.

**Lenient pastes:** send `url` URL-encoded or not (unencoded query parts are read back into it; `page` stays this endpoint's own parameter). A missing
scheme, a `www.`, bare or `m.` host, quotes or a label around it, trailing punctuation, a Markdown, Slack or Jira link,
percent-encoding and text after the address are all read. The address ends at the first space, line break or `|`; a
line break that plainly cuts it is joined back.

**Refused with a 400** that names what to use instead:

- another site; a course page (→ `/course-details-by-url`), a job or company page;
- a provider profile, awarding-body, subject-directory, sign-in or account page;
- a bare number (a course_id → `/course-details`);
- two different Reed addresses (the same one twice counts once), or an address broken off.

